# Milestones and documentation

## Workflow

1. Write Plan sections in `docs/milestones/M<N>-<slug>.md` first (including **Testing**).
2. Wait for explicit user **approved** before coding that milestone.
3. After implementation:
   - In **chat**: highlight review-worthy code (citations), explain what changed and why.
   - In **docs**: fill Results (including Testing results), append `LEARNING_LOG.md`, update `docs/architecture.md` if topology changed.
   - **Concept Q&A:** prepend/update English Q→A in `LEARNING_LOG.md` for doubts raised in the review chat (and core “why / without it” for that milestone). See `.cursor/rules/learning-log-qa.mdc`.
   - Land **unit + integration tests** for code added in this milestone (see `docs/notes/testing.md`).
4. Commit + **push to `origin`**, then do not mark Done until the close-out checklist passes.
5. **Before starting the next milestone Plan (hard gate):**
   - Working tree must be **clean** (`git status` empty of staged/unstaged/untracked work that belongs in the repo).
   - Local branch must be **synced with remote** (no unpushed commits for the closed milestone).
   - If anything is dirty or unpushed: **commit + push first**, then write the new Plan.
   - Also point the user at the prior milestone’s Learning Log Q&A; wait for them to be ready.

## Required sections in every milestone file

- Status, Goal, Why this milestone, Concepts introduced
- Design decisions & alternatives considered
- **Architecture graph (planned)** — Mermaid; freeze after approval
- **Testing (planned)** — concrete unit cases + integration cases (skip rules if no key/service)
- Tasks, Demo / acceptance criteria
- **Results** with all of: What we did; Commands & how to reproduce; **As-built graph** + delta; Why this approach; Deviations; Pitfalls; **Testing results**; Open questions / next dig

## Testing (mandatory every milestone)

- Unit: no network; covers new pure/branching behavior.
- Integration: real provider or Compose where relevant; skip if unavailable, but tests must exist.
- Milestone is not Done if new production code has no matching tests.
- Strategy: `docs/notes/testing.md`.

## Graphs (mandatory)

- Plan graph before approval; Results as-built graph after coding (or note "unchanged").
- From M2+: include LangGraph node/edge topology (Mermaid; optional `draw_mermaid()` paste).
- Chat diagrams are ephemeral — copy into the milestone file.
- `docs/architecture.md` = current state only; milestone files = history.

## Close-out checklist

- Plan approved before coding (including Testing plan)
- Implementation landed
- Unit tests green; integration tests present (skip OK without creds/services)
- Chat review handover: highlighted code + what/why explained
- Results complete (commands + why + graphs + testing results)
- LEARNING_LOG.md entry added (**including Concept Q&A** from review chat — see `learning-log-qa.mdc`)
- architecture.md updated if needed
- Changes committed (English message) and **pushed to GitHub**
- `git status` clean and branch not ahead of `origin` for that close-out
- Stop and wait for next approval (user studies Learning Log before the next Plan)
- **Do not draft the next milestone Plan until the previous close-out is committed and pushed**

## Simplifications

Label teaching shortcuts as **simplification** and note what production would still need.
